Package: anchoredRI
Type: Package
Title: Estimate Reference Intervals Using Clinically Screened Observations
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Amrom", "Obstfeld", role = "cre",
    email = "13033252+amromeo@users.noreply.github.com",
    comment = "Research question and repository owner"),
    person("OpenAI ChatGPT", role = "aut",
    comment = "AI system that generated the project materials"))
Description: Research software for estimating a reference distribution in one or two
    clinical settings using a small, independently screened reference sample.
    Fits semi-supervised Gaussian and shifted-lognormal mixtures with
    setting-specific proportions, model selection and bootstrap intervals.
    Includes paired simulations and optional comparisons with 'refineR'
    (Ammer et al. (2021) <doi:10.1038/s41598-021-95301-2>).
    An AI system developed the code, tests, simulations and documentation
    in response to a human research question. Evaluated on synthetic data.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, utils, parallel
Suggests: refineR (>= 2.0.0)
URL: https://amromeo.github.io/anchoredRI/,
